{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/907544-whw-s-setting-hacks-and-houserules-2nd-edition","id":907544,"title":"WHW's Setting Hacks and Houserules; 2nd Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-05T02:47:34-07:00","id":907544,"title":"WHW's Setting Hacks and Houserules; 2nd Edition","content":"Basically, a place for me to drop my homerules and setting changes, so people can tell me implications I've overlooked or tell me why it's a bad idea.<br /> <br /> <b>DISSONANCE CHANGE: RATIONALIZATION IS MAGIC</b><br /> Dissonance doesn't obscure supernatural. It obscures Supernal Magic, and Supernal Magic only. Rationalization will follow the path of least resistance, depending on each victim individually - this means that for a devout Catholic, Magic might look like Miracles; for UFO geek, like Alien Tech; and so on. <br /> Why? Because it makes covering your track as a Mage harder, allows for fucked up cults where Mage pretends to be a god figure while casting in front of &quot;his&quot; Sleepers, and makes Hunters really dangerous. It also allows for Sleeper pawns that won't forget their orders or role, as long as they are properly indoctrinated; a Sleeper Servant will really believe that you are his Lord and Master, and will aid you in your Heavenly War of Gods (read, Consilium business), he will just see everything through different lenses. <br /> Yes, Mages are dicks and their servants are really low on Integrity. It's intended!<br /> <br /> <b>GNOSIS DISTRIBUTION: GNOSTIC REVELATION IS HARD</b><br /> Most common Gnosis rating in the game is 1 and 2. For most of characters, Gnosis is permanently locked at 3. Gnosis of 4 is extremely rare, and you probably could gather all Gnosis 5 Mages in the world in one room. Gnosis of 6 and more is Archmage territory. No character may purchase Gnosis above 3 without unraveling unique mystery (read: you need a plot milestone and GM approval).<br /> Why? Because we like smaller scale and lower power levels. It also creates interesting consequence for Legacy Teaching, forcing Mages to rely on Soul Stone and Daimonicon methods much more than on simply (&quot;simply&quot;) grabbing a tutor. <br /> <br /> <b>CRAFT YOUR OWN LEGACY!</b><br /> As long as you do enough research, creating your own Legacy, or creating novel Attainments for existing one is equal XP wise to following orthodox path. You may freely modify Primary and Optional Arcanum of your Legacy, as long as it makes sense.<br /> Why? We aren't very attached to idea of Mages gathering around Legacies, and prefer image of solitary Mages doing their own personal research much more. Individualism, ho! Pre-existing Legacies are still a strong pick, due to their social benefits. Charging less XP for unorthodox Attainments means more variety between Legacy Members, allowing them to be dramatically different in their approach, even if they share the ideology. This also means that it isn't that uncommon for Cabals with strong Cabal Symbolism to develop &quot;Cabal Legacies&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>HORIZONTAL GROWTH: ATTAINMENTS</b><br /> Because Mages will be stuck at low Gnosis, they need an alternative way to continue pursuing magical research. This is done by allowing developing extra Utility Attainments for their Arcana. Difference between a Gnosis 1 Apprentice with Death 3 and Gnosis 3 &quot;Master&quot; with Death 3 is going to be the fact that &quot;Master&quot; developed fuckaton of Attainments to personalize his magical style.<br /> This also helps me with the problem of &quot;All mages with Arcanum X can cast all spells, how do I give them limitations on what they can do?&quot;. <br /> Why? Because we love horizontal growth.<br /> <br /> <b>CONDITIONS ARE MAGIC</b><br /> All Spells are Conditions and Tilts. Period. Psychic Domination? &quot;Psychic Domination&quot; Condition. Frogification? &quot;Frogification&quot; Condition. And so on. This means they can sometimes be ended early, and you *can* Pattern Bolster them away.<br /> Why? Because it makes stuff like Psychic Domination less insane against Mages. <br /> <br /> <b>PATTERN BOLSTERING BOLSTERED</b><br /> Pattern bolstering removes any Condition or any Tilt. However, Environmental Tilts and Persistent Conditions will reapply next turn. Pattern Bolstering takes effect immediately, even if you can't spend all the needed Mana, but you are *forced* to use following turns to pay for it. <br /> Why? Because solving all your problems with Pattern Bolstering isn't as fun as it sounds, but solving some obnoxious one is good. Giving you Pattern Bolstering immediately helps with stupid annoying instant kill tactics and rocket tag problems that are rather relevant at low Gnosis.<br /> <br /> <b>SOUL STONES FOR EVERYONE</b><br /> Cool shit happens when Soulstones are stolen. In order for them to be stolen, people need to actually *use them* and *carry them*. Each character starts with one Soulstone for free. This is often an item that soaked all the superduper energy from their Awakening. Additionally, using Soulstone always considers you to be &quot;a Mage of equal Gnosis&quot;.<br /> Why? Because we want each character to have a signature item of power, and we want people to use them. <br /> <br /> <b>ENVIRONMENTAL YANTRA? WHAT'S THAT?</b><br /> Environmental Yantras don't exist, because literally no one used them. Instead, symbolically powerful Environment can buff your persona Yantra by 1. This cannot be combined with other ways to buff your Persona.<br /> Why? Because with 2 Yantra Slots, people basically did this: Persona for 3, High Speech or Soulstone for 2, ignore all +1 Yantras forever.<br /> <br /> <b>EXPERIMENTAL: LEGACY YANTRAS? WELL...</b><br /> Legacy Yantras that are are appropriate for your Persona can be used as your Persona Yantra, with +1 bonus on top. This may not be combined with other ways to buff Persona. You can Legacy Yantra normally, too.<br /> Why? Same reason Environmental Yantras needed to be recalibrated. Also, because most characters will have only 2 or 3 Yantra slots available, all of the small +1 Yantras simply *won't be used*, as everyone and their dog is going to grab Persona, High Speech and some +2 Yantra, ignoring +1 Tools forever. <br /> <br /> <b>EXPERIMENTAL: PATH OR ORDER TOOLS? WELL...</b><br /> Using a Tool can buff your Persona bonus by 1. Can't be combined with other ways to buff Persona. You can still use tools as standalone thing if you have leftover slots.<br /> Why? As above.<br /> <br /> <b>TALKING ABOUT PERSONAS...</b><br /> 1. Renamed from &quot;Shadow Name&quot; to &quot;Persona&quot;<br /> 2. All Mages start with 1 dot in it for free. <br /> <br /> <b>APOSTATE AND NAMELESS EQUALITY</b><br /> Characters without Order training start without Rotes, 1 Status Merit, Order Tools and so on, and get XP refund for it that can be only spent on Merits. Characters in Orders can do this to show their incomplete training, and they can also customize 1 order rote skill. <br /> <br /> More will might come later, will get edited in + posted as a standalone post. Feel free to comment. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T03:33:07-07:00","id":907554,"title":"","content":"I very like Dissonance change, as I marked it earlier - it does have sense setting-wise. And leads to interesting implications. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Rest... Seems to be too hard-coded - you have Persona Yantras for 3 and Soul Stones for 2 as mage - cool, more to you. But using Environment or Tools Yantras maybe more handy in some instances than yelling 'I'm Thor. god of thunder' and then smiting your enemy with lighting. I just say that variety of Yantras can lead players in to more creative usage of their environment ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) on game sessions. Higher Yantras bonus makes Persona and Soul Stone still more desirable thing for players to have.<br /> <br /> As to Gnosis - I go about those guidelines, setting-wise, but still do not limit players mechanically. PC in game world are always exceptional, in the end. And let them have high Gnosis - when they get Paradox, it will sting them harder. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T03:55:00-07:00","id":907558,"title":"","content":"They want to have high powered options gate locked because they don't want to accidentally move into high tier game mode. I know, it's weird, but they don't want to be all powerful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. And special milestone requirement makes them feel more special and cool about getting that dot. It also helps when designing NPCs, because it forces you to think about an answer to the question of &quot;what allowed this person to break through the gnostic gate?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T07:23:19-07:00","id":907618,"title":"","content":"I really, really like the &quot;Rationalization is Magic&quot; hack, though I'm not totally sure it's actually a hack so much as a slight shift in emphasis on something that's already part of canon. Either way, I'm definitely a fan.<br /> <br /> I also rather like Gnostic Revelation is hard, as I generally prefer to run low-mid tier games where power stat 5 is the highest you usually see, and 6+ being the stuff of urban legend. By extension, Horizontal Growth: Attainments is something I would consider using.<br /> <br /> Craft Your Own Legacy is also very much my style, and seems like the more practical way to go at least until we've got more example legacies to draw from.<br /> <br /> The rest are not really to my taste, but it seems like you've got a good idea of what your group needs and how you're going to deliver it. Good luck, and thanks for sharing!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T08:10:34-07:00","id":907639,"title":"","content":"Hey WHW,<br /> <br /> I really like these House Rules, and I am going to adopt those into my game now. <br /> <br /> Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T11:18:30-07:00","id":907751,"title":"","content":"I dig the idea of someone having a Soulstone tied to the moment of their Awakening, I have to admit. May borrow that one myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T13:01:10-07:00","id":907812,"title":"","content":"To me it looks more like Persona is your problem, rather than the others. I mean, your legacy yantra, order and path tools should really fit into it anyway.<br /> <br /> I supposed you could replace the cap on yantra use with a cap on the different types of yantra. That way making the correct environment is always beneficial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T09:28:31-07:00","id":908383,"title":"","content":"I liked the Conditions are Magic one, though I am going to think of a better way to phrase it. <br /> <br /> I also think the Rationalization one is more a matter of emphasis rather than house ruling, but I do like it. <br /> <br /> Pattern Bolstering is interesting too, makes it more useful. <br /> <br /> I have been working on alternate ways to solve the issue with Shadow Name and make Yantras more diverse in general. I think the answer lies to making the Shadow Name merit work differently, rather than make more stuff tack on to it. Making it free... might be good or bad, I am not sure yet. I will think about it.<br /> <br /> Stuff about Apostates and Nameless, sounds good on paper, but I kinda dislike having too many Apostates running around in my games and this kind of encourages it. So, I guess its a matter of taste. <br /> <br /> The other rules didn't interest me as much. Thanks for sharing them anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T08:35:53-07:00","id":909187,"title":"","content":"My problem with current Pattern Bolstering is that it's too slow in turn-by-turn situations unless you achieved Gnosis 3, and it's pretty easy to inflict scene-deciding tilt or condition. I don't like Rocket Tag (whoever wins initiative gets to decide outcome of the scene by virtue of taking first action) and Counterspelling is very impotent, so Bolstering upfront and putting you into Mana Debt is a good compromise. And of course, Mana Debt (&quot;get healed now, spend next X turns paying for it&quot;) is great, because it makes Mage hemmorage Mana like crazy. Starting Mage will get dry after purging 3 tilts, which is...very quickly. <br /> Getting into Mana Debt also means you can't pay Mana to reduce Paradox, so inflicting Tilts on your Mage opponent still has tactical value - you might not take them out in the single turn, but you are doing damage and putting them in a bad spot. <br /> I ignored the Physical Tilt/Mental Condition rule because it creates weird situations where Tilts turn into Conditions out of combat and vice versa.<br /> <br /> Persona being powerful is a good and bad thing for us, because we want to encourage Persona more than we want to encourage other Tools, mostly because Persona is self-limiting. It creates patterns, and patterns create vulnerabilities, and allow playing around them. Magic in Mage is very broad; by making your most powerful Yantra one that forces you to follow certain restrictions, you are willingly limiting what kind of Magic you can work with efficiently. Fire focused Mage won't be as effective at Wind Magic, for example, and thus is probably going to stick to Fire based soluitions, which in turn makes it possible to play around that and expect him to use fire spells. <br /> <br /> Well, half of the starting Cabal is Nameless and they decided to do that before we did that homerule,so yeah :P. In general, we don't perceive Pentacle as designated Protagonists, and they often end up being straight out antagonists.<br /> <br /> Here are some interesting setting consequences arising from the Gnosis Cap:<br /> <br /> 1.Magic at level 4 becomes incredibly rare and precious. What kind of magic it is?<br /> - HEALING MAGIC. Lethal and Aggravated Damage is hard to heal without easy access to 4th dot of Magic! Mages thus have to rely on Medical Care, Accelerated Healing Times, and Pattern Bolstering to deal with lethal wounds, unless they can find a Mage willing to use their healing spells on them.<br /> <br /> - Teleportation. Simply Teleporting in and out is harder. This makes Orders less global and makes travel plots actually viable.<br /> <br /> - Removing Curses and Vile Destinies that are not results of Supernal Magic (because those you can, you know, just Dispel) becomes super hard, because you both have to find an Adept of Fate, AND perform spell-dictated quest.<br /> <br /> - Oaths are much more binding. While it's still easy to dispel them, actually modyfing them is really, really hard now.<br /> <br /> - Imbued Items become much more valuable, simply because there is a lot less Mages capable of creating them. Same thing about Fetishes.<br /> <br /> - And so on...<br /> <br /> 2. Because Adept Magic is much harder to get your hands on, it increases value of alternate means of getting these effects done. Artifacts that grant their users access to Adept level Magic are incredibly potent and desirable; some Consilia are going to rely on Artifacts to provide some of their services or estabilish infrastructure, and these thingss getting destroyed or stolen might...cause...problems<br /> <br /> 3. This should get it's own entry later, but basically, Quintessences. Sometimes, Mages really really really want to cast that 4/5 dot spell once. And...it's possible. Kinda. Sort of. By solving a special Mystery, Mages may try to arrange special circumstances that will allow one shot casting of a spell beyond their understanding. Obviously, each such solution is highly unique and basically a plot point that might take days, months or years to put in motion; they always require great deal of sacrifice and work. They don't have a general mechanic, because each case is unique.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T06:18:18-07:00","id":910017,"title":"","content":"After having some fun with the idea of multiple Attainmens, I really like how it's working. Relatively newbie Mages feel like humans with magical powers, but the more experienced ones, ones who invested in the Attainments, start to really drift away from their human self. I think it really helps hammer the idea that Mages can become disqualified from being humans by their own choice; Unleashing Spells didn't really work here (too easy to Dispel, too easy to make these changes inherent parts of the character); Attainments that are, for lack of better comparison, kind of like Ordo Dracul's Coils and Scales push the angle of &quot;look what you can become&quot; really well without being too pushy or overpresent. I also like how they tend to make you grow horizontally (allowing them to do more stuff and or in different ways), instead of vertically (making all your stuff more powerful), so even an &quot;Elder&quot; Mage with a whole gauntlet of Attainments doesn't feel oppressively overpowered in a way that Adept and Master Arcana wielding Mages do.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Also, because a lot of them require Mana upkeep (even if it's something like 1 mana per day), it ramps up and makes more inhuman mages more and more reliant on stable sources of Mana, which in turn makes Mana even more valuable; it actually gives them ways and reasons to constantly be at Mana deficit, never stabilizing at a &quot;comfortable living standard&quot;, because <i>you can be so much more</i>. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 06-08-2016, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T13:06:30-07:00","id":914306,"title":"","content":"We decided that following things can be bought <b>only</b> by Arcane XP:<br /> Arcanum Dots <br /> Gnosis<br /> Rotes<br /> Praxes<br /> Attainments<br /> blatantly Supernal Merits<br /> <br /> Additionally, we don't charge XP for restoring Wisdom; fulfilling a Wisdom Obssession restores you a point. This is due to using Group Beats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T14:24:01-07:00","id":914367,"title":"","content":"Would love to hear more about the custom Attainments your players make. Explain what differentiates them from Praxes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T14:29:12-07:00","id":914371,"title":"","content":"Praxis would be a spell you specialize in. Attainment would be either a perk you can apply to your Spell Casting (something that modifies the way you interact with magic), or changes you in some manner. &quot;Can drink blood of others to regain Mana, as if it was a form of Pattern Scouring&quot; could be an example of what we are aiming at. Things that aren't fitting to be spells, especially spells that anyone can cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:49:18-07:00","id":914595,"title":"","content":"I like the soul stone change, hate the dissonance and low gnosis crap change because it alters things to a Mage game I used to play and no longer like. The rest? Meh, or haven't thought it through yet. I also like the Wisdom buy back because it allows for you to be going down the path of hubris and still get &quot;Come to Jesus&quot; chances with the chance to reassess more often. <br /> <br /> At least you're brave enough to put your house rules out there for the masses. Good stuff man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 06-14-2016, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:28:42-07:00","id":914615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/907544-whw-s-setting-hacks-and-houserules-2nd-edition#post907544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, a place for me to drop my homerules and setting changes, so people can tell me implications I've overlooked or tell me why it's a bad idea.<br /> <br /> <b>GNOSIS DISTRIBUTION: GNOSTIC REVELATION IS HARD</b><br /> Most common Gnosis rating in the game is 1 and 2. For most of characters, Gnosis is permanently locked at 3. Gnosis of 4 is extremely rare, and you probably could gather all Gnosis 5 Mages in the world in one room. Gnosis of 6 and more is Archmage territory. No character may purchase Gnosis above 3 without unraveling unique mystery (read: you need a plot milestone and GM approval).<br /> Why? Because we like smaller scale and lower power levels. It also creates interesting consequence for Legacy Teaching, forcing Mages to rely on Soul Stone and Daimonicon methods much more than on simply (&quot;simply&quot;) grabbing a tutor.<br /> <br /> <b>HORIZONTAL GROWTH: ATTAINMENTS</b><br /> Because Mages will be stuck at low Gnosis, they need an alternative way to continue pursuing magical research. This is done by allowing developing extra Utility Attainments for their Arcana. Difference between a Gnosis 1 Apprentice with Death 3 and Gnosis 3 &quot;Master&quot; with Death 3 is going to be the fact that &quot;Master&quot; developed fuckaton of Attainments to personalize his magical style.<br /> This also helps me with the problem of &quot;All mages with Arcanum X can cast all spells, how do I give them limitations on what they can do?&quot;.<br /> Why? Because we love horizontal growth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am a big fan of either depowering mage or better yet horizontal Growth, im looking forward to read more on this. I will say though, i dont know if in 2ed Gnosis is as much as a stick to meassure high/low powered scale. You do indeed get lots of reach/yantras/praxies for the gnosis but also is your gnosis as paradox the one you get hit when you overreach.<br /> <br /> I havent take the game for a spin yet so maybe is my impression that arcanum dictates more the power scale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/907544-whw-s-setting-hacks-and-houserules-2nd-edition#post907544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>SOUL STONES FOR EVERYONE</b><br /> Cool shit happens when Soulstones are stolen. In order for them to be stolen, people need to actually *use them* and *carry them*. Each character starts with one Soulstone for free. This is often an item that soaked all the superduper energy from their Awakening. <u><b>Additionally, using Soulstone always considers you to be &quot;a Mage of equal Gnosis&quot;</b></u>.<br /> Why? Because we want each character to have a signature item of power, and we want people to use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont get the bold part, What you mean by it? As for soul stones. I use them A LOT, as in &quot;its one of the main themes in my games&quot; in 1E, so what i suggest is reading the alternatives uses in Tome of Mysteries and boost them to make them worthy.<br /> <br /> Ex: In 1E, i made that your tool made of your soul stone gave you Gnosis/2 rounded down in free points of spell factors (in 2e it would be reach, i guess but them i would recommend gnosis/3).<br /> <br /> Antidemesnes gave you a -gnosis of the creator as penalty for the arcanum of his choosing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T17:16:41-07:00","id":927845,"title":"","content":"In 2nd ED, Soul Stones are useable as a Yantra Tool. If &quot;creator's Gnosis is equal to user's Gnosis&quot;, it gives +2; if it's bigger than your Gnosis, it gives you +3. We ruled that you are always considered to be equal to your own Gnosis when wielding your own Soul Stone.<br /> <br /> Field trip report:<br /> Soul Stones work great so far. It works much better than Dedicated Tool at giving each Mage their personal item of power, and people had a blast figuring out what their free Soul Stone could be.<br /> <br /> I mentioned in another thread that we wanted to limit Wisdom sins only to Magic, but after reading some disucssion here, I asked for a trial period for rules as written Wisdom. And it works! Players actually want to provoke Wisdom Rolls, because it gives them beats, and Wisdom Rolls give you a way to actually get Arcane Beats from non magical activities. Go figure.<br /> <br /> Fate Magic gives me so much headaches that I sometimes I wish I didn't pick an Acanthus, because I constantly need to constraint my spellcasting due to obvious ways to both unravel the plot and steal spotlight from other characters. It stresses me out, I don't like self policing like that. <br /> <br /> After some tinkering, we decided to ignore Nimbus Tilts for next few sessions, because they are annoying to apply (another roll to add to the routine), never work anyway, and their mechanical representation doesn't mesh very well with Nimbus Descriptions of the players.<br /> <br /> <br /> Are there any questions about our game? I like answering questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T09:49:48-07:00","id":929255,"title":"","content":"Could you kindly provide further explanation of your &quot;Conditions is Magic&quot; hack? I am intrigued by this idea but I'd like to know how example conditions might look, especially conditions. Also, more on how this hack changes gameplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T12:44:25-07:00","id":929905,"title":"","content":"I'll give some examples tommorow probably. We have them noted, but as we play in Polish, I need to translate them into English before posting. <br /> As for changing the gameplay - it basically makes tracking spells much easier, and allows to have some &quot;expend this condition to gain X&quot; effects that would look weird as a part of a spell.<br /> Ok, I'll do one quick:<br /> <br /> Looking Good!<br /> Source: Matter Magic (Find The Balance spell)<br /> By using an unholy alliance of good fashion sense, alchemical taste and mysteries of Stygia, you make your looks more than good - you made them enchanting. You may expend this Condition to catch eye of a target NPC and make him impressed.<br /> Resolution: Magic wears off, expend as in description, spill your drinks<br /> <br /> This is what our Moros wanted to do with a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T20:23:37-07:00","id":934875,"title":"","content":"One of consequences of our low-powered world is that number of Mages capable of creating Rotes is very, very small. This should mean that Rotes are not very diverse, and are quite rare.<br /> This isn't necessarily what we wanted, so solution at which we arrived is the following:<br /> While there are Rotes created by mortal Mages, a lot of them come from different sources. Sometimes, pursuing an Obsession results in a Mysterious Revelation that allows the Mage to glimpse a formula for Rote; other Rotes are extracted from ancient (or futuristic) sources. And, most reliably, a Mage can work with Supernal Entity they Summoned to learn a Rote expressed by the Being.<br /> <br /> Basically, Mages may excuse their Rote purchases by interacting with their Summons. Does it deemphasize Orders? A little. Order will just give it to you; Supernal Being? It will either challenge you to a quest, or will require your help to &quot;birth&quot; their Rote.<br /> And of course, you can't use this method if you can't Summon Arcanum-synched Being. So if you really want that Forces Rote, maybe ask you Order, probably someone else had similar idea, and then pooled the Rote in Order Pool.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Also, for many Mages, Summoned Being is their first &quot;mentor&quot; - due to decreased Mage Density, it might take months or years for you to meet other Awakened; and because many Mages either start, or quickly arrives at 3rd dot of their Arcanum, gaining intuitive understanding of summoning...it doesn't take long before their first summoning circles is created, and something appears in it to answer questions dripping from their mouth.<br /> In fact, many Mages join their Orders after being taught by their Supernal Advisor, when they grow lonely enough - or scared enough - to ask &quot;Am I the only one?&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Other task that Supernal Beings can perform to compensate for lower &quot;mastery bar&quot; in Arcana, is creating Familiar Bonds. Get a willing Spirit/Ghost/Goetia, face a Trial from Rank 4 being, enjoy your Familiar Bond.<br /> Familiar bond also &quot;ascends&quot; the familiar, making it little more...human that it's non familiar kin; Spirit starts to become something more than what they symbolize, and Ghost gains potential to outgrow being an echo without turning into a monstrosity of Rank3+ Ghosts. Why? Maybe it's the Supernal Spark that lies at the foundation of the bond, or maybe because by being so Close sympathetically to a human, they start being a little human themselves.<br /> [Why from meta point of view? Because we like our Familiars to actually have a personality, be their own person, and that's usually reserved for Rank3+ beings. Which can't be Familiars.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-21-2016, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:20:04-07:00","id":943870,"title":"","content":"Veiling spells are kinda nuts. So, we are attempting to tone them down a little, specifically the &quot;mundane attempts to perceive the subject automatically fails&quot;.<br /> What do you think about following solution(s)?<br /> <br /> Solution a: When something would draw subject's attention to the item (for example, a police man is searching a crime scene that contains the item, or invisible gun is being used to shoot people), mundane people can perceive it at Potency penalty <br /> <br /> Solution b: Instead of above, any attempts to perceive veiled stuff using mundane means require Exceptional Success to succeed.<br /> <br /> Solution c: Make one of above default way, and add another one as a Reach effect.<br /> <br /> Solution d: B+A = When not grabbing attention it requires ExSuccess, when specifically looked for, it penalizes by Potency.<br /> <br /> I personally like b the most, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}